# Story 43: Raw Mode & Escape Hatch (45s)
# Hook: In raw mode every key goes to the program. Ctrl+O is your escape hatch back to Rysh.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-043-raw-mode-escape-hatch.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
In raw mode every key goes to the program. Ctrl+O is your escape hatch back to Rysh.

[00:03.0 --> 00:07.0]
Start rysh, then open an interactive program.

[00:07.0 --> 00:15.0]
Open vim. On the alternate screen, the pane enters raw mode -- Tab, brackets, Escape, every key is forwarded straight to vim.

[00:15.0 --> 00:27.0]
So how do you reach Rysh's own shortcuts? Ctrl+O. It's the one key raw mode reserves -- the escape hatch out to prefix mode, even while a program owns the screen.

[00:27.0 --> 00:34.0]
From prefix mode you can detach with d, or press any other key to cancel and drop right back into the program.

[00:34.0 --> 00:42.0]
Back in vim, quit the usual way -- colon-q-bang to discard.

[00:42.0 --> 00:45.0]
Raw mode keeps programs happy; Ctrl+O keeps you in control.

